spec ww05-update-delete-chain-commit: 2 sessions, 10 permutations
# WW05, commit arm. s1 updates n then deletes it in ONE transaction and commits; s2,
# whose snapshot predates s1's commit, writes n.y. s2 is refused whenever s1's chain
# is in flight or committed after s2's snapshot.

starting permutation: s1u s1d s1c s2w s2c
step s1u: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.x = 1 RETURN n.x AS x
x
-
1
(1 row)
step s1d: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) DETACH DELETE n RETURN count(*) AS deleted
deleted
-------
1      
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2w: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.y = 1 RETURN n.y AS y
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: COMMIT
ERROR: cypher: transaction poisoned by a prior failed Exec statement — call Rollback
final final: MATCH (n:Item) RETURN n.name AS name, n.x AS x, n.y AS y ORDER BY name
name|x|y
----+-+-
